{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01UyU3YbJhnE69mgzLz9eBPL","type":"tool_result","content":"0\t---\n1\ttype: Reference\n2\ttitle: Background commands\n3\tdescription: How an agent declares background commands so a running build holds its task active, and how a hook-driven declaration is wired.\n4\ttags: [agents, activity, background-shells]\n5\tsources:\n6\t  - resource: src/main/agent/shared/background-command-hooks.ts\n7\t  - resource: src/main/agent/shared/background-shell-hint-hook.ts\n8\t  - resource: src/main/agent/agent-adapter.ts\n9\t    title: backgroundCommands\n10\t---\n11\t# Background commands\n12\t\n13\tA background command the agent starts (a build, a test run, a dev server) holds its task `thinking` until the command exits, so a task never reads idle while its work runs. A command that is meant to stay up, a server or a watcher, is released by the agent with `kangentic_mark_background_service`, or kept out of the hold from the start by `--kangentic-no-activity-hold` in its command. Both end the hold without stopping the process. The engine side is in [Activity Detection](../../activity-detection.md), \"Opting a background shell out of the hold\".\n14\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3712ca08-51d7-4376-98cc-deee7ebb9910","uuid":"e35390fd-9b4d-4573-8b54-afdb34a9c0d5","timestamp":"2026-10-22T22:46:44.034Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"__CHECKOUT__\\docs\\integrations\\agents\\background-commands.md","content":"---\ntype: Reference\ntitle: Background commands\ndescription: How an agent declares background commands so a running build holds its task active, and how a hook-driven declaration is wired.\ntags: [agents, activity, background-shells]\nsources:\n  - resource: src/main/agent/shared/background-command-hooks.ts\n  - resource: src/main/agent/shared/background-shell-hint-hook.ts\n  - resource: src/main/agent/agent-adapter.ts\n    title: backgroundCommands\n---\n# Background commands\n\nA background command the agent starts (a build, a test run, a dev server) holds its task `thinking` until the command exits, so a task never reads idle while its work runs. A command that is meant to stay up, a server or a watcher, is released by the agent with `kangentic_mark_background_service`, or kept out of the hold from the start by `--kangentic-no-activity-hold` in its command. Both end the hold without stopping the process. The engine side is in [Activity Detection](../../activity-detection.md), \"Opting a background shell out of the hold\".\n","numLines":15,"startLine":0,"totalLines":53}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01UyU3YbJhnE69mgzLz9eBPL","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
